course: dictionary
lesson: 6791
title: Orchard: a place of fruit trees
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An orchard is a piece of land with many fruit trees, like apple, pear, cherry or orange trees. The trees are often planted in neat rows, so you can walk between them.
explain: Look at the clues in «wet orchards», which sits near meadows, ponds and streams in the countryside. Those clues tell you an orchard is outdoors, on land, not a room or a shop.
explain: Now read «the Death-or-Glory Toads would storm the orchard!» Storm here means attack, so an orchard can be a place where a story's battle happens. Put your meaning in the sentence, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: An orchard is a piece of land with many fruit trees.
fact: Orchards often have trees planted in rows.
fact: Apple, pear, cherry and orange trees can all grow in an orchard.
fact: Bees visit the blossom in an orchard, so the fruit can grow.
fact: Farmers grow the same kind of apple tree by grafting: a twig from a good tree is joined onto young roots.
exercise: What is an orchard? | A busy road for cars | *A piece of land with many fruit trees | A kind of bird's nest | A large lake with boats on it
exercise: A farmer plants 4 rows of cherry trees in an orchard, with 5 trees in each row. How many trees are there? | 45 | 9 | 4 | *20
exercise: Bees visit the blossom in an orchard. Why? | *To help the fruit grow | To build a home for the trees | To steal the blossom | To make the orchard quieter
test: «The apple trees in the orchard were covered in pink blossom.» Where do these trees grow? | In a kitchen | *In an orchard | In a river
test: The Toads plan to «storm the orchard». What does storm mean here? | *Attack | Water | Count | Sleep
exam: Which of these would you find in an orchard? | A flock of sheep in a barn | *Rows of cherry trees | A school bus | A railway station
